    "mapping_notes": "# cutlass86_blackwell_mixed_dtype_gemm.compute_100a\n\n## Reference interface\n\nAll indices below are logical indices. Byte-level layout information from the\nsaved optimized input is retained in source_interface.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Logical shape | Role | Optimized counterpart |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A | bf16 | 128 x 128 | input | logical activation A |\n| B | uint8_t | 256 x 64 | input | logical weight B; reference rows are output channels |\n| D | bf16 | 128 x 256 | output | D |\n| scale | bf16 | 256 x 1 | input | per-output-channel, per-K-group weight scale |\n\n## Computation and mapping\n\nThe reference uses A[m,k], B[n,k], and D[m,n]; B is stored with output-channel first.\nB is canonical signed INT4: even k in the low nibble, odd k in the high nibble.\nweight[n,k] = signed_int4(B[n,k]) * scale[n,k/128].\nD[m,n] = sum_k A[m,k] * weight[n,k]. No zero-point is used.\nThe selected SM100 source uses signed int4 with contiguous K coordinates.\nThe byte mapping preserves the two adjacent nibbles; signed decoding remains\npart of the expressions. No host-side weight permutation is applied by this mapping.\nScale layout [n,k_group] is the transpose of source [k_group,n] storage.\nThe optimized mainloop swaps/transposes operands. The reference restores\nactivation-first GEMM; its M/N names are the public mathematical M/N names.\nThe saved epilogue uses alpha=1 and beta=0; C is not read.\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nThe PyTorch reference is `reference.py`, with explicit argument bindings in\n`reference_binding.json`: BF16 activation A, packed signed INT4 B, BF16 scale, and\nthe full 128 x 256 BF16 output. The scale-only scenario has K=128 and one scale per\nchannel. This is not a comparison against a GPU execution. Arithmetic uses the\nideal-real contract; precision differences are not checked bitwise.\n\nRun the reference with:\n\n```sh\nsentryward corpus/cutlass86_blackwell_mixed_dtype_gemm.compute_100a.ptx \\\n  --input examples/cutlass86_blackwell_mixed_dtype_gemm.compute_100a/input.json \\\n  --reference examples/cutlass86_blackwell_mixed_dtype_gemm.compute_100a/reference.py \\\n  --reference-binding examples/cutlass86_blackwell_mixed_dtype_gemm.compute_100a/reference_binding.json \\\n  --timeout 1200 > output.json\n```\n\nThis runs verification and reference equivalence together on the saved input.\n\n## Upstream\n\n- https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/blob/e64a9136dd929639e5f7c969fe5af3bf7415cd4f/examples/86_blackwell_mixed_dtype_gemm/86_blackwell_mixed_dtype.cu\n- https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/blob/e64a9136dd929639e5f7c969fe5af3bf7415cd4f/include/cutlass/gemm/kernel/sm100_gemm_tma_warpspecialized_mixed_input_transform.hpp\n"
  },
